claims.statement_original:
Assume Condition 1 holds and $v_2\asymp1$. Let $\beta^*,d^*$ and $\gamma^*$ be as in (2.6), and $N,L\geq3$ satisfying $(NL)\asymp\{n/\log^6(n)\}^{\nu^\dagger/(4\gamma^*+2\nu^\dagger)}$ for $\nu^\dagger=1-1/p$. Consider the approximate least squares estimates with optimization error bounded by $\delta_{n,\mathrm{LS}}^2$, where $\delta_{n,\mathrm{LS}}\asymp\{\log^6(n)/n\}^{\gamma^*\nu^\dagger/(2\gamma^*+\nu^\dagger)}v_p^{1/(2p)}$ and the depth and width of the network class $\mathcal F_n=\mathcal F_n(d,\bar L,\bar N,M)$ satisfy (3.15). Then, for all sufficiently large $n$, the following bound
\[
\sup_{\substack{f_0\in\mathcal H(d,l,\mathcal P)\\\mathbb E[\varepsilon\mid X]=0,\mathbb E[|\varepsilon|^p\mid X]\leq v_p}}
\mathbb P\left\{\sup_{f\in\mathcal S_{n,\infty}(\delta_{n,\mathrm{LS}})}\|f-f_0\|_2\geq c_7D\delta_{n,\mathrm{LS}}\right\}\leq c_7D^{-2p}
\]
holds for any $D\geq1$, where $c_7$ is a universal constant independent of $(n,D,p,v_p)$.
